{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2184-01-20 01:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee, one of the hospitalists. I understand you came in with abdominal pain and vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2184-01-20 01:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, thank you. The pain came on suddenly this morning. I’ve had Crohn’s for years, and this feels like one of my flares."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2184-01-20 01:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You had a fever earlier too, around 100.5. Any cough, shortness of breath, or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2184-01-20 01:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, no breathing issues. But I did vomit a few times, and I’ve had chills the past couple days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2184-01-20 01:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. The CT scan didn’t show a blockage or new abscess. Your bowel wall thickening is stable. We think this is likely a Crohn’s flare with possible ileus."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2184-01-20 01:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes sense. I’ve been off pain meds for a while, feeling stable, but last week the fevers started."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2184-01-20 01:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re starting IV antibiotics—cipro and flagyl—for now, just in case there’s infection. We’ll also keep you NPO and use the NG tube to help with nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2184-01-20 01:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I placed the NG tube myself in the ER so I could get the CT. It’s uncomfortable, but I know it helps."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2184-01-20 01:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That was smart. We’ll reassess your pain and see if we can ease up on the dilaudid. You’re on the right track."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2184-01-21 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your blood cultures came back negative, which is great—no active bloodstream infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2184-01-21 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. My port’s been okay—no redness or pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2184-01-21 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. Your CRP and ESR are elevated, which supports inflammation, likely from Crohn’s. Stool tests were negative for C. diff and other infections."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2184-01-21 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not an infection, just a flare?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2184-01-21 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s the current thought. But your chest X-ray shows pneumonia in the right lung. Could be from aspiration when you vomited."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2184-01-21 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh. I didn’t even feel like I was coughing it up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2184-01-21 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It can happen silently. We’re switching your antibiotic from cipro to levofloxacin to better cover pneumonia."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2184-01-21 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. Will I need more scans?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2184-01-21 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll repeat the chest X-ray in a few days to check the pneumonia. For now, focus on resting and letting your gut rest."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2184-01-22 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. The new chest X-ray shows the pneumonia is still there, but your oxygen levels are good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2184-01-22 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Any fever?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2184-01-22 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve been afebrile since yesterday. That’s a good sign the antibiotics are working."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2184-01-22 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. My nausea’s still there, but less than before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2184-01-22 07:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep the NG tube for now. GI wants to do a colonoscopy soon to check your bowel health before considering new Crohn’s meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2184-01-22 07:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’d prefer to wait for my regular GI doctor. I don’t want just anyone doing it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2184-01-22 07:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. We’ll coordinate with your GI. In the meantime, we’re keeping you on IV fluids and antibiotics."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2184-01-23 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your urine culture showed contamination, so no UTI. Blood cultures still negative—great news."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2184-01-23 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad it’s not another infection. My port’s been trouble before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2184-01-23 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re monitoring it closely. No signs of infection there. Your hemoglobin dropped a bit, but it’s stable now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2184-01-23 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had iron deficiency for years. I just can’t tolerate oral iron."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2184-01-23 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll continue monitoring. For now, we’re not planning a transfusion."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2184-01-24 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve been passing gas and have some bowel sounds. That’s a sign your ileus is improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2184-01-24 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel like I might be ready to try a little food."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2184-01-24 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll start with clear liquids and see how you do. If that goes well, we can advance to a soft diet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2184-01-25 07:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You tolerated the BRAT diet well yesterday. We’re going to remove the NG tube this morning if you’re okay with it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2184-01-25 07:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Please. I’m tired of it. My nausea’s much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2184-01-25 07:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll do it now. Let us know if nausea returns."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2184-01-26 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your repeat chest X-ray shows the pneumonia is starting to improve."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2184-01-26 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. I feel stronger every day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2184-01-26 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re also restarting your citalopram for anxiety. You mentioned PTSD gets worse in hospitals."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2184-01-26 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it’s hard. I had a bad experience years ago. I declined psych consult, but I’ll take the Celexa."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2184-01-26 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve also prescribed PRN valium if you feel overwhelmed. Social work checked in with you yesterday?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2184-01-26 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, she was very kind. I’m okay for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2184-01-27 20:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The latest chest X-ray shows continued improvement in the pneumonia. Your lungs are clearing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2184-01-27 20:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. I haven’t had any fever in days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2184-01-27 20:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’ll finish the IV antibiotics soon. Now, about the colonoscopy—your GI doctor scheduled it for tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2184-01-27 20:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Finally. I want to make sure it’s him."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2184-01-27 20:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It is. He’ll assess for strictures and inflammation. It’ll help decide if you can start a new Crohn’s medication."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2184-01-28 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The colonoscopy was done. Prep wasn’t ideal, but they saw no strictures or major inflammation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2184-01-28 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So no blockages?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2184-01-28 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "None. That’s good. But because the view wasn’t perfect, they’ll want a repeat when you’re fully recovered."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2184-01-28 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll make sure I prep better next time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2184-01-28 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll help you with that. For now, you’re doing well. You’ve been on a soft diet, and your pain is controlled with oral meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2184-01-29 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow. You’ll go home on oral cipro and metronidazole for 10 more doses."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2184-01-29 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the dilaudid?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2184-01-29 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll have some tablets for breakthrough pain, but we encourage tapering off quickly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2184-01-29 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I don’t want to stay on them. I’ve been off before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2184-01-29 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great. We’ll also send you home with benadryl and Phenergan for nausea, if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2184-01-29 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my port care?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2184-01-29 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue flushing per protocol. We’re concerned about future access, but your surgeon is aware."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2184-01-30 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re cleared to go home. Your pain and nausea are much better, and your pneumonia is resolving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2184-01-30 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m so glad. Thank you for listening to me about my GI doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2184-01-30 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Of course. Follow up with your PCP and GI. Call if you develop fever, worsening pain, or trouble breathing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2184-01-30 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And I’ll restart my Celexa daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2184-01-30 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good plan. Take care, and we’re here if you need us."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2184-01-30 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2184-01-30 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a final check before discharge. Any new symptoms?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2184-01-30 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I feel ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2184-01-30 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. Your instructions are printed. You’re doing well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2184-01-30 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The transport team will take you to your ride in about an hour."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2184-01-30 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Perfect. I appreciate everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2184-01-30 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing—your B12 and thyroid meds should continue as usual."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2184-01-30 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I haven’t missed those."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2184-01-30 13:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. And keep up with the pantoprazole for stomach protection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2184-01-30 13:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2184-01-30 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll call you in a few days to check in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 76,
      "time": "2184-01-30 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. That means a lot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 77,
      "time": "2184-01-30 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your ride is here. Take care and get some rest."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 78,
      "time": "2184-01-30 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 79,
      "time": "2184-01-30 16:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’re glad you’re feeling better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 80,
      "time": "2184-01-30 16:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Me too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 81,
      "time": "2184-01-30 17:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just confirming—you understand when to call the doctor?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 82,
      "time": "2184-01-30 17:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, if I get fever, pain, or can’t keep food down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 83,
      "time": "2184-01-30 17:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. You’re all set."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 84,
      "time": "2184-01-30 18:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Goodbye, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 85,
      "time": "2184-01-30 18:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. See you soon."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2184-01-20 00:40:00",
    "admission_end": "2184-01-30 18:55:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 54-year-old woman with a complex history of Crohn’s disease, multiple abdominal surgeries, short bowel syndrome, and PTSD was admitted for acute abdominal pain, nausea, vomiting, and fever, initially concerning for a Crohn’s flare. Imaging showed no bowel obstruction but revealed aspiration pneumonia in the right lung, which was treated with intravenous levofloxacin. She was managed conservatively for a paralytic ileus with an NG tube, which was later removed as bowel function improved. She tolerated a soft diet and transitioned to oral pain medications. A colonoscopy was performed by her preferred gastroenterologist, showing no strictures or significant inflammation, though the prep was suboptimal. Her anxiety and PTSD were addressed with restart of citalopram and PRN benzodiazepines. She was discharged home in stable condition on a short course of oral antibiotics, with instructions to taper analgesics and follow up with her primary and specialty providers.",
    "problems": [
      "Regional enteritis of unspecified site",
      "Pneumonitis due to inhalation of food or vomitus",
      "Paralytic ileus",
      "Dysthymic disorder",
      "Unspecified acquired hypothyroidism",
      "Posttraumatic stress disorder",
      "Other chronic nonalcoholic liver disease",
      "Iron deficiency anemia, unspecified",
      "Other B-complex deficiencies",
      "Myalgia and myositis, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
